# {{ title }} web

The Next.js front end of {{ title }}. The browser talks only to this server;
route handlers in `app/api` forward to the Keel API (`KEEL_API_URL`) and keep
the JWTs in httpOnly cookies (`lib/bff.ts`).

```sh
cp .env.example .env.local
npm install
npm run dev        # http://localhost:3000, with `keel dev` running in the app root
```

Accounts: `POST /api/auth/register` on the API (when `auth.registration` is
on), then sign in at http://localhost:3000/login.
